{"type":"Feature","properties":{"kind":"port_limits","cargo":[],"osm":["way/182794406"],"source":"Derived: the convex hull of this port's terminals from OpenStreetMap, grown by 200 m, then cut to the water OpenStreetMap maps inside it (the sea within its coastline, rivers, docks and basins), with the terminals kept whole","licence":"ODbL-1.0","reviewed_at":"2026-11-23","clip":"water","note":"OpenStreetMap maps no port limits for Tin Can Island. These are the hull of the island grown by 200 m, cut to the water OpenStreetMap maps inside it, with the island kept whole and a 30 m margin where it meets the water. What is left is the island and the creek and harbour water off its quays, clear of Apapa's limits to the east. The island's own outline holds a 6 ha area OpenStreetMap maps as residential, unnamed, which is inside the limits. Otherwise a scan of OpenStreetMap finds no homes or hospitals inside; across the creek, the shore edges of two unnamed residential areas, the Sea School grounds and Snake Island reach in by about 0.3 ha in all."},"geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[3.330494,6.434299],[3.330886,6.433715],[3.338101,6.428132],[3.343007,6.427478],[3.345758,6.427852],[3.347469,6.428431],[3.348042,6.428726],[3.348418,6.428784],[3.350285,6.430058],[3.350607,6.430002],[3.351106,6.429418],[3.351085,6.429069],[3.350607,6.428512],[3.361226,6.429999],[3.363916,6.43192],[3.364405,6.432668],[3.364543,6.433356],[3.364413,6.434188],[3.363819,6.434607],[3.363697,6.434484],[3.363238,6.434921],[3.363351,6.435054],[3.362643,6.435959],[3.362528,6.435857],[3.362213,6.436295],[3.362321,6.436369],[3.361937,6.43682],[3.361937,6.436985],[3.360647,6.438059],[3.360717,6.438194],[3.360357,6.438526],[3.358104,6.43955],[3.356321,6.439864],[3.355219,6.439866],[3.35348,6.439577],[3.351689,6.438307],[3.349384,6.437114],[3.349364,6.439687],[3.348732,6.439646],[3.348685,6.437117],[3.348568,6.43682],[3.348275,6.436622],[3.347477,6.436449],[3.345063,6.436469],[3.345079,6.436554],[3.34